PentaX modifications, 2026: an original immutable scoped ELF provider,
owner/source/live-marker attestation before library dispatch, checked guest
data reads, bounded batch snapshots and cumulative session limits, synchronous
compiler/Vulkan execution with same-owner fenced writeback, and typed stops
for unsupported queues, commands or resource profiles. No C++ code, game
program or game shader is distributed. Original x64 diagnostic consumers
exercise the four imported functions. Known compute registers now persist
independently per observed ACB queue. Bounded command plans include indirect
call/chain frames and multiple dispatches; same-owner backing checks refuse GPU
writes aliasing captured commands. Failures after possible GPU work are terminal.
Ordered memory writes and fulfilled waits retain the same exclusive owner and
transactional admission; failure after possible guest writes is also terminal.
Indirect arguments are read after earlier effects, with explicit empty outcomes.
Draw queues, asynchronous scheduling, general coherence and presentation remain
unfinished.

AgcSuspendPoint retains per-owner frame-boundary/reset state without clearing
compute queues. The synchronous backend completes fenced GPU work and same-owner
writeback before submission returns, so successful boundaries have no outstanding
prefix to wait for; poisoned partial submissions cannot report success. Boundary
count is not a presented-frame count. Exact Graphics5/Graphics5 and the separately
verified libSceAgc/libSceAgc module/library 1.1/1 spellings are admitted; submit
functions remain in their own Graphics5Driver namespace.

